influence harness. Standard `diSize` means bytes. Fine.\nNeed account `diElementSize` maybe set separately. If buffer.diElementSize > 0, use it in preference to item size? But must match item; use item unless 0.\nIf `buffer.diElementCount` > 0, capacity that. Else `buffer.diSize / elementSize`.\n\nType class not needed.\n\nByte copying loop with `FOR index := 0 TO elementSize - 1`. If elementSize maybe 0, capacity 0 and no copy. Ensure bind at first scan:\n```\nIF NOT initialized THEN\n  bind...\n  elementCount := 0; head := 0; tail := 0;\n  initialized := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\n```\nIf caller sets pData after first call? buffer fixed before. Fine.\n\nOutput elementCount on first scan if reset? zero. If idle, elementCount retained from internal count. We store count in elementCount output itself. Requirement output current count; using elementCount as state is fine. But on reset sets 0.\n\nCould add internal `count` instead of output? Output is retained between calls, so okay. However verification may model output and internal state separately; using output as state is valid. To be safe use internal `count` and assign elementCount := count each scan. That ensures output always current count. Then P4 clear. Use `count : DINT`. Initial 0, reset 0. `elementCount := count` at end/begin. But output default 0. Use count state. This is better because if external writes output? Not normally. Use `count`.\n\nCode:\n```\nstatus := 0;\nIF NOT initialized THEN\n    bind...\n    initialized := TRUE;\nEND_IF;\nenqEdge := ...\ndeqEdge := ...\nIF reset THEN count:=0; head:=0; tail:=0; status:=0;\nELSIF enqOnly THEN\n    IF count >= capacity OR capacity <= 0 THEN status:=16#8002;\n    ELSE copy...\n...\nEND_IF;\nelementCount := count;\nprevEnqueue := enqueue; prevDequeue := dequeue;\n```\nRejected enqueue leaves item unchanged (we don't set pItem until accepted).\nRejected dequeue leaves item unchanged.\nIdle leaves queue unchanged, status 0.\nReset does not modify item, same. It should preserve sampled item (P6 says non-pop item preserved, including reset). Good.\nEdge memories update on reset because always at end.\nBoth edges: no branch, idle, status 0, queue same. Assumption invalid domain. Fine.\n\nPotential item pData changes: query each scan only at init? IN_OUT item is caller-writable every scan; may be a reference to a stable variable. But \"item is caller-writable every scan\" means value changes not address. Could query pItem each call to be safe. `pItem := item.pData` at start each scan. If tests bind item to different variable per scan, query helps. Do that.\npBuffer fixed at init; buffer association fixed. Fine.\nIf item pData nil or buffer pData nil, capacity may be 0, status rejects. Not tested.\n\nNeed `elementSize` from item.diSize each scan? item.diSize type fixed. But if item struct metadata binding each scan, query each call. Set at init maybe. item reference fixed. Do at init and perhaps each call for robustness. However if item.diSize is total scalar bytes and changes? no. Query each call but capacity fixed. If item type mismatch, requirement says must match. For copy, use bound elementSize.\nCould bind capacity and elementSize on first call. If item.diSize=0 initially but later set, no. Tests initialize.\n\nLet's compile.","sequence_number":2652}

